// Shared tier: idle. Wander to a spot the host picked, then wait a random time there; a replan in the middle of the
// wait keeps waiting instead of picking a new spot.
//
// Teaches: a re-entrant behaviour driven by a timer fact (the first branch is "a wait is already running"), a
// target chosen by a host sensor instead of a planning-time operator, an always-true last branch that takes time.
// Source: Space Station 14 (MIT), `IdleCompound` in Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/idle.yml at commit
// 614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d:
// https://github.com/space-wizards/space-station-14/blob/614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d/Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/idle.yml
// Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2017-2026 Space Wizards Federation; see src/examples/canon/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
// Adapted (YAML prototypes re-written in our domain language). Constants are SS14's blackboard defaults
// (NPCBlackboard.cs: MinimumIdleTime 2, MaximumIdleTime 7).
// Emulations (our planner has no planning-time effects):
// - SS14 `PickAccessibleOperator` writes a reachable spot into the blackboard while planning; here a host sensor
//   publishes `(idle_spot ?spot)`, a random reachable spot within the idle range, before the plan.
// - SS14 `RandomOperator` + `WaitOperator` roll the time while planning, then wait it out; here one primitive,
//   `!idle_wait ?min ?max`, rolls the time when it starts and writes `(idle_until ?t)`, which the host removes when
//   the time is up. That fact is what SS14's `KeyExistsPrecondition IdleTime` reads in the first branch.
// Deviations: a third branch `stay_put` (SS14 has two): when the creature is buckled or pulled, or the host found no
// spot, SS14's `IdleCompound` fails and the root has nothing left; ours waits in place, so the tier always plans.
// Not ported: `IdleSpinCompound` (the turret's idle: spin to a random angle), the `IdleRange` key (it is the host
// sensor's radius).
//
// Facts:      (now ?seconds) clock; (idle_until ?seconds) a running idle wait; (idle_spot ?spot) host sensor;
//             (buckled), (pulled) body state.
// Primitives: (!wait_until ?seconds) (!move_to ?spot) (!idle_wait ?min_seconds ?max_seconds)

(:domain idle

    (:constants IdleTier
        (idle_min 2.0)
        (idle_max 7.0)
    )

    // An idle wait started earlier is still running; ?out_until is when it ends.
    (:axiom (idle_timer ?out_until)
        (and
            (idle_until ?out_until)
            (now ?n)
            (< ?n ?out_until)
        )
    )

    // Contract: takes some seconds and never fails.
    (:method (idle)

        (keep_waiting
            (and
                (#idle_timer ?until)
            )
            (
                (!wait_until ?until)
            )
        )

        (wander
            (and
                (not (buckled))
                (not (pulled))
                (idle_spot ?spot)
            )
            (
                (loiter_at ?spot)
            )
        )

        (stay_put
            ()
            (
                (!idle_wait @idle_min @idle_max)
            )
        )
    )

    // Walk to ?inp_spot and wait a random time there. Shared with the follow tier.
    (:method (loiter_at ?inp_spot)

        (go_and_wait
            ()
            (
                (!move_to ?inp_spot)
                (!idle_wait @idle_min @idle_max)
            )
        )
    )
)
